    "notes": "Read 2026-10-11, 2026-10-20 and 2026-10-21: labeled Public preview, preview terms (API version 2026-09-30.preview), no price on the docs pages. The price, 0.15 USD per SPT issued, is on Stripe's US pricing page (src-openai-acp-stripe-pricing), listed since at least 2026-04-23; its Learn more link opens the agent variant of this page. On 2026-10-20 the seller variant adds the SPT Resolve API (a granted token resolved once into fpan, network_token, agentic_token or dpan credentials for a third-party processor, encrypted unless the seller has given Stripe a PCI Attestation of Compliance), lists consumed, resolved, expired or revoked as deactivation reasons, and names American Express ACE Kit beside Mastercard Agent Pay and Visa Intelligent Commerce; the agent variant still names Mastercard and Visa only and says consumed, expired or revoked. The Wayback capture of the seller variant's .md on 2026-09-21 (timestamp 20260921161216) has neither 'resolved' nor 'American Express', so both additions date to between 2026-09-21 and 2026-10-20. Same URL as src-stripe-spt in the openai-acp dossier (visa-tap uses that id for a Stripe blog post, so a new id is used here)."
